# ── Server-side environment variables (for the API server) ──
#
# These are set on the VPS as environment variables (NOT in the client bundle).
# They are used by the Express API server (server/index.js) to authenticate
# with the GitHub API. The PAT never reaches the browser.
#
# Create a fine-grained Personal Access Token at:
#   https://github.com/settings/tokens?type=beta
# Repository access: "Only select repositories" → pick this repo
# Permissions: Issues → "Read and write"
#
# Set these on the VPS (e.g., in /etc/environment, .env file, or docker-compose.yml):
# GITHUB_PAT=github_pat_...
# GITHUB_REPO=Pradyu12/InfoSecure
#
# For local development with docker-compose, copy this to .env (no quotes needed):
# GITHUB_PAT=github_pat_...
# GITHUB_REPO=Pradyu12/InfoSecure
